# Onec Context Bundle

Run the tools from this bundle's directory. Python 3.11+ and Zstandard support
must already be available; this bundle does not bootstrap an environment.
Read [README](README.md) for runtime requirements.

## Resolve and query

```sh
python3 tools/resolve_packs.py --bundle-dir .
```

Choose the configuration and version before a target-bound lookup. Resolve a
role with `--role` and, when needed, `--target`; `--path-only` returns the path
for a reader's `--db` argument. Never guess filenames.

| Role | Reader | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `platform` | `tools/local_kb_query.py` | Versioned platform API |
| `standards` | `tools/local_kb_query.py` | ITS development conventions |
| `metadata` | `tools/local_kb_query.py` | Objects, fields, types and forms |
| `code` | `tools/query_code_pack.py` | Modules, symbols and call relationships |
| `full` | `tools/query_config_pack.py` | Exact source files |

For knowledge packs, use `--q`, `--exact`, `--json` and the required `--version`.
Without `--exact`, search uses exact matches first and then lexical FTS5.
`--detail full` returns the preserved extracted record. Separate examples use
`--domain api_examples`. Neither mode guarantees complete original HTML coverage.
Use the reader's `--help` before unfamiliar operations.

## Interpret evidence

Cite relevant topics, versions and source paths. Separate facts from deductions.
A code index is not a runtime execution trace. No result means unconfirmed in the
selected pack. Run the project's diagnostics and tests after changes to code.

The map stores common roles in `packs.platform` and `packs.standards`; project
roles are in `targets.*.packs.metadata`, `code` and `full`. Layers can be absent.
This bundle has no `scripts/onec_context.py`, `ensure` or build tools. If data is
missing or stale, report the gap and prepare a new export with the toolkit.

